From c2cb44b1d1f0e29aa96c191976b37dd60a29e9e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gvirabyan21 <gvirabyan21@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:53:32 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Serve Unity Ads directly in the Android app's Armenian mode

AdMob's policies forbid ads beside Armenian content, so the Android app
in Armenian showed no ads at all. It now leaves AdMob unstarted and
calls Unity Ads directly through a small Android-only method channel,
on an interstitial placement of its own. Russian, English and all of
iOS keep AdMob with its mediated networks, unchanged.

A hand-written channel rather than a Flutter plugin: the plugins ship an
iOS copy of the Unity SDK via Swift Package Manager, which would clash
with the CocoaPods one the AdMob Unity adapter already brings. The app
depends on the same Unity SDK version as that adapter.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
